# Brewfile.vscode — VS Code extension list, NOT loaded by default.
#
# Split out of the main Brewfile on 2026-08-22. Visual Studio Code is no longer
# installed on this machine (Cursor is the editor in use, and /usr/local/bin/code
# was a dangling symlink into the removed app). `brew bundle`'s `vscode` directive
# shells out to the `code` CLI, so with VS Code absent all 117 entries below made
# `brew bundle check` permanently unsatisfiable — a manifest that can never be
# satisfied stops being a useful check.
#
# Kept rather than deleted: this is a real record of extension preferences, and
# Cursor can consume the same identifiers.
#
# To restore into the main Brewfile:      cat Brewfile.vscode >> Brewfile
# To install them into Cursor instead:    grep -o '"[^"]*"' Brewfile.vscode | tr -d '"' \
#                                           | xargs -n1 cursor --install-extension
# To install into VS Code once reinstalled: brew bundle --file=Brewfile.vscode
